From e776b823c9ae18830094ac1c3c8552242c7aefc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Stankewitz <daniel@voukoder.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:48:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] avcodec/hap: add Hap R (BC7) encoding and decoding

Hap R stores RGBA frames as BC7 (BPTC) textures, FourCC Hap7, top-level
section types 0xAC, 0xBC and 0xCC.

Add a BC7 block encoder that uses all eight block modes. Opaque blocks
are coded with modes 0, 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6 and keep alpha at exactly 255,
blocks with transparency use modes 4, 5, 6 and 7 including channel
rotation and index selection. The partitions of the multi-subset modes
are ranked with an error estimate derived from the principal axis of each
subset, the best candidates are encoded with least squares endpoint
refinement and an exhaustive p-bit search.

The encoder is selected with -format hap_r and supports the snappy and
none second-stage compressors and chunking like the other Hap formats.

Add a BC7 block decoder to texturedsp and Hap7 to the Hap decoder and the
mov tag table, so that Hap R files can be probed and decoded.
